                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Jeffery",
                        "email": "andrew@codeconstruct.com.au",
                        "username": "amboar"
                    },
                    "message": "Hi Brad, thanks for the patch. I have a few comments inline."
                },
                {
                    "file": "include/libpldm/base.h",
                    "line": 729,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Jeffery",
                        "email": "andrew@codeconstruct.com.au",
                        "username": "amboar"
                    },
                    "message": "Is this true?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "include/libpldm/base.h",
                    "line": 729,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Brad Bishop",
                        "email": "bradleyb@fuzziesquirrel.com",
                        "username": "bradbishop"
                    },
                    "message": "it is not.  will remove."
                },
                {
                    "file": "include/libpldm/base.h",
                    "line": 729,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Brad Bishop",
                        "email": "bradleyb@fuzziesquirrel.com",
                        "username": "bradbishop"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                },
                {
                    "file": "include/libpldm/base.h",
                    "line": 734,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Jeffery",
                        "email": "andrew@codeconstruct.com.au",
                        "username": "amboar"
                    },
                    "message": "Do you have thoughts on how we track what it's replacing? I'm torn between asking that you mark `decode_multipart_receive_req()` as deprecated now, and the opposition to doing so because this new API is not yet marked as stable."
                },
                {
                    "file": "include/libpldm/base.h",
                    "line": 734,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Brad Bishop",
                        "email": "bradleyb@fuzziesquirrel.com",
                        "username": "bradbishop"
                    },
                    "message": "FWIW I don't see any users of the old API on Github.  I do plan to eventually add an in-library user of the new one - would stabilizing it then break the rules?  I wouldn't think this new API is going to require lots of iterating to get right."
                },
                {
                    "file": "include/libpldm/base.h",
                    "line": 734,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Jeffery",
                        "email": "andrew@codeconstruct.com.au",
                        "username": "amboar"
                    },
                    "message": "Skiboot and hostboot?\n\nhttps://github.com/search?q=decode_multipart_receive_req&type=code&p=1"
                },
                {
                    "file": "include/libpldm/base.h",
                    "line": 734,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Brad Bishop",
                        "email": "bradleyb@fuzziesquirrel.com",
                        "username": "bradbishop"
                    },
                    "message": "Right I saw those, but I thought they were just embedded/vendored libpldm forks, and I didn't see any actual users.  Did I miss it?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "include/libpldm/base.h",
                    "line": 734,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Jeffery",
                        "email": "andrew@codeconstruct.com.au",
                        "username": "amboar"
                    },
                    "message": "In my mind that doesn't disqualify them from consideration. Perhaps there are circumstances around those projects where they won't see a lot of activity, but I don't think that means we should ignore them. We should offer them the usual upgrade path.\n\nFor replacing APIs, I think I've landed on asking for the deprecation/removal patches to be pushed on top of the patch adding the new API, but marked as WIP. That way we've always got a reference for what needs to be done.\n\nAre you happy to do that?\n\nFWIW, I'll tag a release whenever we want to remove something. I don't have any requirements around minimum time or amount of change between tags."
                },
                {
                    "file": "include/libpldm/base.h",
                    "line": 734,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Brad Bishop",
                        "email": "bradleyb@fuzziesquirrel.com",
                        "username": "bradbishop"
                    },
                    "message": "> Are you happy to do that?\n\nyes.  I took a crack at those:\n\nhttps://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/libpldm/+/91952/1\nhttps://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/libpldm/+/91953/1"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/dsp/base.c",
                    "line": 627,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Jeffery",
                        "email": "andrew@codeconstruct.com.au",
                        "username": "amboar"
                    },
                    "message": "You can re-arrange this so the complete comes first and then you can skip the `pldm_msgbuf_discard()` calls:\n\n```suggestion\n\trc = pldm_msgbuf_complete_consumed(buf);\n\tif (rc) {\n\t\treturn rc;\n\t}\n\n\tif (req->transfer_opflag > PLDM_XFER_CURRENT_PART) {\n\t\treturn -EPROTO;\n\t}\n\n\t// DSP0240 v1.2.0 \u00a79.6.5 Table 17: transfer_handle must be non-zero\n\t// only when operation is PLDM_XFER_NEXT_PART.\n\tif (req->transfer_handle == 0 &&\n\t    req->transfer_opflag == PLDM_XFER_NEXT_PART) {\n\t\treturn -EPROTO;\n\t}\n\n\treturn 0;\n}\n```"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/dsp/base.c",
                    "line": 627,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Brad Bishop",
                        "email": "bradleyb@fuzziesquirrel.com",
                        "username": "bradbishop"
                    },
                    "message": "Nice, will do."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/dsp/base.c",
                    "line": 627,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Jeffery",
                        "email": "andrew@codeconstruct.com.au",
                        "username": "amboar"
                    },
                    "message": "The other thing to note with the msgbuf APIs is that if you use an extracted value, you should test the result of its specific extraction to ensure you won't read uninitialised memory. The compiler will optimise away the unnecessary checks, so my preference is to just test everything you need to use."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/dsp/base.c",
                    "line": 627,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Brad Bishop",
                        "email": "bradleyb@fuzziesquirrel.com",
                        "username": "bradbishop"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                }
            ],
